---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const title = "Rent vs Buy Down Payment (Tradeoffs and impact)";
const description =
  "How down payment size affects rent vs buy results, PMI, and opportunity cost. Educational use only.";
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/guides/rent-vs-buy-down-payment">
  <section class="card hero">
    <span class="pill">Guide</span>
    <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Home</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/guides">Guides</a>
      <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span aria-current="page">Down payment</span>
    </nav>
    <h1>Down payment tradeoffs in rent vs buy</h1>
    <p>
      A bigger down payment can lower your mortgage payment and reduce interest, but it also ties up cash that could be invested.
      This guide shows how to model both sides of that tradeoff.
    </p>
    <div class="btn-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/rent-vs-buy-calculator">Rent vs buy calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/topics/rent-vs-buy">Rent vs buy topic hub</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">What changes with a larger down payment</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Lower loan balance and monthly principal and interest.</li>
      <li>Potentially lower rate and lower mortgage insurance costs.</li>
      <li>Less cash available to invest or keep liquid.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">PMI and thresholds</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      If your down payment is below a lender threshold, mortgage insurance can add to monthly costs. Model PMI as an added monthly
      cost in the rent vs buy calculator so the comparison stays realistic.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Opportunity cost</h2>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0">
      Any extra cash used for the down payment is cash that cannot be invested elsewhere. Use the investment return input to model
      what that cash could earn if you rented instead.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Scenario template</h2>
    <ol class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Run a base case with your likely down payment.</li>
      <li>Run a higher down payment scenario (lower rate and payment).</li>
      <li>Run a lower down payment scenario (higher payment + PMI).</li>
      <li>Compare total cost and break-even across scenarios.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Common mistakes</h2>
    <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
      <li>Ignoring PMI or assuming it is negligible.</li>
      <li>Using the same investment return for all scenarios without adjusting risk.</li>
      <li>Not accounting for reduced liquidity after a large down payment.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">FAQ</h2>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Is a larger down payment always better?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      Not always. It lowers payment and interest, but it can reduce liquidity and investment opportunities.
    </p>
    <h3 style="margin:12px 0 0">Should I use retirement savings for a down payment?</h3>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:8px 0 0">
      This guide does not provide financial advice. Model the opportunity cost and consult a qualified advisor if needed.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="grid" style="margin-top:18px">
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/calculators/rent-vs-buy-calculator">Rent vs buy calculator</a></li>
        <li><a href="/calculators/mortgage-payment-calculator">Mortgage payment calculator</a></li>
        <li><a href="/calculators/amortization-schedule-calculator">Amortization schedule</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="card section prose col-6">
      <h2 style="margin-top:0">Related guides</h2>
      <ul class="muted" style="margin:10px 0 0; padding-left:18px">
        <li><a href="/guides/rent-vs-buy-checklist">Rent vs buy checklist</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/rent-vs-buy-investment-return">Investment return assumptions</a></li>
        <li><a href="/guides/pmi-removal-vs-extra-principal">PMI removal vs extra principal</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="card section prose" style="margin-top:18px">
    <h2 style="margin-top:0">Next steps</h2>
    <div class="btn-row" style="margin-top:10px">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/calculators/rent-vs-buy-calculator">Run the calculator</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/rent-vs-buy-checklist">Rent vs buy checklist</a>
      <a class="btn" href="/guides/rent-vs-buy-break-even">Break-even guide</a>
    </div>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0">Educational use only. Not financial advice.</p>
    <p class="muted" style="margin:12px 0 0; font-size:13px">Last updated: 2026-01-30</p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
